Usage: logger [OPTION]... [MESSAGE]

Write messages to the Windows event/logging facilities.

OPTIONS:
  -i, --id            log the logger command's PID
  -f, --file ARG      log the contents of this file
  -e, --skip-empty    do not log empty lines when processing files
  -p, --priority ARG  message priority
  -s, --stderr        also write the message to standard error
  -t, --tag ARG       mark every line with this tag
  -n, --server ARG    write to this remote syslog server
  -P, --port ARG      use this port for UDP or TCP connection
  -T, --tcp           use TCP only
  -d, --udp           use UDP only
      --prio-prefix   look for a prefix on every line read from stdin
      --no-act        do everything except the write the log
  -S, --size ARG      maximum size for a single message
      --rfc3164       use the obsolete BSD syslog protocol
      --rfc5424       use the syslog protocol (default for remote)
      --help          display this help and exit
  -V, --version       output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
